# Vauxhall Zafira B seven-seat MPV, 2005-2014.
#
# The second Zafira: the larger, more rounded body with the same Flex7
# seating, sold from 23 July 2005. It was not withdrawn in 2011 but stayed on
# sale alongside the Zafira Tourer until 2014.
# https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Opel_Zafira
#
# Dimensions 4.467 x 1.781 x 1.635 m, wheelbase 2.703 m (Vauxhall Zafira
# brochure, December 2007, 2008 Models Edition 2, dimension drawing).
#
# Shape reference: image 1 is a true level side elevation; the flank is
# traced from it.
#
# Colours: grade (a), the Vauxhall Zafira October 2007 brochure for model
# year 2008: Royal Blue and Flame Red solid; Star Silver, Silver Lightning,
# Moonland and Metro Blue metallic; Peacock, Panacotta, Ultra Blue, Black
# Sapphire and Steel Blue pearlescent. Weights 12, 10, 9, 8, total 39,
# provisional.
# Speed 200 km/h. Comfort 75/443, on the line 330 + 1.5 x 75. Classes 1,2.
# Dates: intro July 2005; retires staggered 2014-2017 as a road tail.
#
# Metres master: citycars/4.5/vauxhall-zafira-b.blend. Interchange:
# citycars/4.5/vauxhall-zafira-b.dae. References:
# citycars/references/vauxhall-zafira-b/ (gitignored).
#
# Accepted deviations: the pre-facelift exterior represents the range. The
# Flex7 seating is not modelled behind the opaque glazing; the mirror
# projection, lamp internals and hatch recess are simplified, and the rear
# glass has a more angular lower edge than the photographs.


